{
  "id": "htb-autopwn-0001-main-workflow",
  "name": "htb-autopwn",
  "description": "Master HTB workflow - orchestrates full attack chain from recon to root",
  "flowchart": {
    "blocks": {
      "start-001": {
        "id": "start-001",
        "type": "start",
        "name": "START",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 50
        }
      },
      "setup-001": {
        "id": "setup-001",
        "type": "prompt",
        "name": "SETUP WORKSPACE",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 150
        },
        "prompt": "Setting up workspace for HTB challenge.\n\nTarget: $1\nChallenge name: $2\n\nCreate any missing directories:\n  ./htb-targets/$2/\n  ./htb-targets/$2/scans/\n  ./htb-targets/$2/loot/\n  ./htb-targets/$2/exploits/\n  ./htb-targets/$2/notes/\n  ./htb-targets/$2/.venv/\n\nSet up Python environment:\n- Use uv to create/sync a venv: cd ./htb-targets/$2 && uv venv\n- You can install any packages needed later with: uv pip install <package>\n- Common packages for exploitation: requests, pwntools, paramiko, impacket\n\nIf ./htb-targets/$2/notes/session.md doesn't exist, create it with:\n- Target IP: $1\n- Challenge: $2\n- Start time: (current timestamp)\n\nConfirm setup is complete.",
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "workspacePath": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "setupComplete": {
              "type": "boolean"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "workspacePath",
            "setupComplete"
          ]
        },
        "sound_effect": null
      },
      "check-state-001": {
        "id": "check-state-001",
        "type": "prompt",
        "name": "CHECK STATE",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 225
        },
        "prompt": "Check what work has already been completed for $2.\n\nCheck for these files:\n1. ./htb-targets/$2/services.json - if exists, recon is done\n2. ./htb-targets/$2/vulns.json - if exists, research is done\n3. ./htb-targets/$2/session-log.md - read to see previous attempts\n\nIf files exist, read them to load context.\n\nReturn:\n- needsRecon: true if services.json doesn't exist or is incomplete\n- needsResearch: true if vulns.json doesn't exist or is incomplete\n- attemptNumber: 1 (or higher if resuming)\n- contextSummary: what's been done so far",
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "needsRecon": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "needsResearch": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "attemptNumber": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "contextSummary": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "needsRecon",
            "needsResearch",
            "attemptNumber",
            "contextSummary"
          ]
        },
        "sound_effect": null
      },
      "refresh-001": {
        "id": "refresh-001",
        "type": "refresh",
        "name": "REFRESH STATE",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 262
        }
      },
      "branch-recon-001": {
        "id": "branch-recon-001",
        "type": "branch",
        "name": "NEEDS RECON?",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 300
        },
        "condition": "needsRecon"
      },
      "recon-001": {
        "id": "recon-001",
        "type": "command",
        "name": "RUN RECON",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 300
        },
        "command_name": "htb-recon",
        "arguments": "$1",
        "inherit_variables": true,
        "merge_output": true
      },
      "save-recon-001": {
        "id": "save-recon-001",
        "type": "prompt",
        "name": "SAVE RECON",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 450
        },
        "prompt": "Recon phase complete for $1 ($2).\n\nTasks:\n1. Move services.json to ./htb-targets/$2/services.json if not already there\n2. Move recon-report-$1.md to ./htb-targets/$2/scans/recon-summary.md\n3. Check if ./htb-targets/$2/session-log.md exists:\n   - If it exists: Read it to see previous progress, then append new recon entry\n   - If it doesn't exist: Create it with header:\n\n# HTB Session Log: $2\n\n## Target Information\n- IP: $1\n- Challenge: $2\n- Started: <current timestamp>\n\n## Progress Log\n\n### [timestamp] RECON COMPLETE\n- Services found: {{services}}\n- Service count: {{serviceCount}}\n\n4. Update ./htb-targets/$2/notes/session.md with recon results\n\nConfirm files are in place.",
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "savedTo": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "recommendedVector": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "attemptNumber": {
              "type": "integer",
              "default": 1
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "savedTo",
            "recommendedVector",
            "attemptNumber"
          ]
        },
        "sound_effect": null
      },
      "refresh-002": {
        "id": "refresh-002",
        "type": "refresh",
        "name": "REFRESH STATE",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 487
        }
      },
      "branch-research-001": {
        "id": "branch-research-001",
        "type": "branch",
        "name": "NEEDS RESEARCH?",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 525
        },
        "condition": "needsResearch"
      },
      "research-001": {
        "id": "research-001",
        "type": "command",
        "name": "RUN RESEARCH",
        "position": {
          "x": 400,
          "y": 500
        },
        "command_name": "htb-research",
        "arguments": "$1",
        "inherit_variables": true,
        "merge_output": true
      },
      "exploit-loop-001": {
        "id": "exploit-loop-001",
        "type": "prompt",
        "name": "EXPLOIT LOOP",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 650
        },
        "prompt": "Exploitation phase for $1 (challenge: $2).\n\nYou have up to 5 attempts to exploit the target. Current attempt: {{attemptNumber}} (default 1 if not set).\n\nFirst, load context from target directory:\n1. Read ./htb-targets/$2/vulns.json to see available vectors\n2. Read ./htb-targets/$2/session-log.md to see what's been tried\n3. Check ./htb-targets/$2/exploits/ for existing exploit scripts\n\nPython Environment:\n- A venv is available at ./htb-targets/$2/.venv/\n- Install packages as needed: cd ./htb-targets/$2 && uv pip install <package>\n- Run scripts with venv: cd ./htb-targets/$2 && .venv/bin/python3 exploits/<script>.py\n- Common packages: requests, pwntools, paramiko, impacket, beautifulsoup4\n\nThen execute exploitation:\n1. Find the highest priority UNTESTED vector (tested=false)\n   - Priority: severity (critical>high>medium>low), then confidence\n2. If no untested vectors remain or attemptNumber > 5, return continueLoop=false\n3. Research the CVE/vulnerability - search for public POCs, exploit-db entries\n4. Write a Python exploit script to ./htb-targets/$2/exploits/<vector-name>.py\n   - Install any needed packages with uv pip install\n   - Use requests for HTTP, pwntools for shells\n   - Script should be standalone and runnable\n   - Include automatic flag capture if possible (search for user.txt, root.txt)\n5. Execute the exploit: cd ./htb-targets/$2 && .venv/bin/python3 exploits/<script>.py\n6. Analyze the output:\n   - Did we get a shell?\n   - Did we capture any flags?\n   - What user are we running as?\n7. Update vulns.json: set tested=true and result=\"success|failed|error: <reason>\"\n8. Append to ./htb-targets/$2/session-log.md with timestamp and results\n9. Return structured output\n\nBe completely autonomous - make all decisions yourself.",
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "exploitSuccess": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "flagCaptured": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "shellObtained": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "currentUser": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "attemptNumber": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "vectorTested": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "continueLoop": {
              "type": "boolean"
            },
            "summary": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "exploitSuccess",
            "attemptNumber",
            "continueLoop",
            "summary"
          ]
        },
        "sound_effect": null
      },
      "refresh-003": {
        "id": "refresh-003",
        "type": "refresh",
        "name": "REFRESH STATE",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 700
        }
      },
      "branch-continue-001": {
        "id": "branch-continue-001",
        "type": "branch",
        "name": "CONTINUE?",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 750
        },
        "condition": "continueLoop"
      },
      "post-exploit-001": {
        "id": "post-exploit-001",
        "type": "prompt",
        "name": "POST EXPLOIT",
        "position": {
          "x": 400,
          "y": 800
        },
        "prompt": "Exploitation succeeded for $1 ($2)!\n\nCurrent state:\n- Shell obtained: {{shellObtained}}\n- Flags captured: {{flagCaptured}}\n- Current user: {{currentUser}}\n\nTasks:\n1. If we have a shell, enumerate the system:\n   - whoami, id, hostname, uname -a\n   - Look for user.txt and root.txt\n   - Check sudo permissions\n   - Look for interesting files\n2. Save any captured flags to ./htb-targets/$2/loot/\n3. Update session-log.md with final results\n4. Write a final summary to ./htb-targets/$2/notes/session.md\n\nProvide completion summary.",
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "userFlag": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "rootFlag": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "finalSummary": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "finalSummary"
          ]
        },
        "sound_effect": null
      },
      "end-001": {
        "id": "end-001",
        "type": "end",
        "name": "END",
        "position": {
          "x": 200,
          "y": 900
        }
      }
    },
